<!--
   QML card deck style "Discworld".

   A parchment face with a gold frame in the palette of the Discworld table
   style (data/gfx/qml/table/discworld/). The index at the top left deliberately
   keeps the original glyphs of the default deck (rank + classic suit symbol),
   so that the cards stay readable at the table without having to get used to
   anything; only the large motif at the bottom right is exchanged.

   Motifs: spades carries the wizard, clubs the Death of Rats, diamonds the
   watchman Nobby Nobbs, hearts the witch Nanny Ogg.

   All four come from bitmap vectorisations (1.4-2.3 MB, 3016-6787 paths);
   inlined 13 times that would be a good 20 MB per suit. For the cards the
   geometry is therefore reduced to motif size: seam strokes removed, curves
   flattened, simplified via Douglas-Peucker and subpaths below a minimum area
   discarded - indistinguishable at motif size, but 13-20 times smaller.

   The values are in source units and have to be adapted to the bounding box
   rather than copied blindly: the target is a tolerance of about 0.27 px in the
   rendered motif. On a 1024x1536 drawing area that means tolerance 3 / area 60
   (Nobby, the wizard); the Death of Rats comes from a 1024x1024 area and
   therefore runs at 2.5 / 40. Despite the same area as Nobby, Nanny needs the
   threshold 30 - at 60 the light frets of her banjo neck disappear and the neck
   looks black.

   Compared to the default deck the index is enlarged by a factor of 1.3 (rank
   scale 0.5733 on anchor 25/10.6, suit symbol 0.5603 on 25/70.72): the detailed
   motifs draw the eye, an index at original size looks too small next to them.
   In exchange the motifs are 10 per cent smaller.

   The anchors are set so that the ink has 6 units of distance to the inner
   frame (x=4.6) on the left as well as at the top. What counts is the widest
   glyph across all 52 cards - the club symbol; whoever changes the anchors
   measures the bounding box of the ink, not the group coordinates.

   Placement: bottom edge y=160, right edge x=106 (hearts), x=112 (diamonds),
   x=114 (spades, clubs). Diamonds stays just below 114, because otherwise
   Nobby's lantern hook almost sticks to the inner frame (x=115.4).
   Scaling is done against the actual bounding box of the motif SVG, not against
   its drawing area - otherwise motifs with a margin look smaller than the rest.
   Heights: Nobby 110, Nanny 99, wizard 94, Death of Rats 94. Nobby runs the
   largest, because as a narrow figure with a lot of air between body and
   lantern staff he would look smaller otherwise.

   Two special cases:
   - The magic staff sticks out beyond the figure at the top left and comes too
     close to the index group (at x=106 it even overlaps it from height 108 on).
     The wizard therefore sits at x=114 and is the only one scaled
     anisotropically - 6 per cent narrower at full height (ratio 0.07337 to
     0.07805). 6 per cent cannot be seen on the figure, from about 12 per cent
     on it looks visibly squeezed.
   - The Death of Rats is a diagonal, nearly square composition and, at 95 wide
     to 94 high, the widest motif. It reaches up to x=19; more height would make
     it run out of the card on the left.

   Do not estimate the upper limits, measure them: render the index groups and
   the motif group separately onto transparency, binarise the alpha, multiply -
   overlapping pixels > 0 means too large.

   Engine index -> card (see CardImage.qml):
     Suit = floor(index / 13): 0-12 diamonds(♦), 13-25 hearts(♥), 26-38 spades(♠), 39-51 clubs(♣)
     Rank = index % 13:        0=2, 1=3, … 8=10, 9=jack, 10=queen, 11=king, 12=ace
-->
<PokerTH>
  <CardDeck>
     <StyleDescription value="Discworld (QML/SVG)" /><!-- Shown in the style selection -->
     <StyleMaintainerName value="PokerTH Development Team" />
     <StyleMaintainerEMail value="webmaster@pokerth.net" />
     <StyleCreateDate value="19.07.2026" />
     <PokerTHStyleFileVersion value="2" />
     <Preview value="preview.png" /><!-- Preview image (landscape only - no portrait needed) -->
     <BigIndexesActionBottom value="0" />
  </CardDeck>
</PokerTH>
